'''Marino Girolami''' (1914 – 1994) was an Italian film director and actor.

==Biography==
Marino Giorlami was born in 1914.{{sfn|Curti|2015|p=55}} Formally a [[Professional boxing|Professional boxer]], Girolami entered into Italy [[Centro Sperimentale di Cinematografia]].{{sfn|Curti|2015|p=55}} He debuted as an actor in 1940, and became an assistant director for [[Mario Soldati]], [[Marcello Marchesi]], [[Vittorio Metz]].{{sfn|Curti|2015|p=55}}{{sfn|Curti|2015|p=56}} In 1949 he debuted as a director with [[La starda buia]], a variation on the film ''[[Fugitive Lady]]''.{{sfn|Curti|2015|p=56}} he followed the film with several musical comedies and melodramas.{{sfn|Curti|2015|p=56}}

Film historian and critic Roberto Curti described Girolami as one of Italy's most prolific genre directors, directing 78 films in three deacdes.{{sfn|Curti|2015|p=55}} Girolami worked in several genres and trends such as the Western with ''[[Between God, the Devil, and the Winchester]]'', the crime film (''[[Violent Rome]]'') and horror with ''[[Zombie Holocaust]]''.{{sfn|Curti|2015|p=55}}{{sfn|Curti|2015|p=56}} Girolami also made [[hardcore pornography]] such as ''[[Sesso profondo]]''.{{sfn|Curti|2015|p=56}} Girolami died in 1994.{{sfn|Curti|2015|p=55}}

==Personal life==
Girolami was the older brother of director Romolo Girolami, who worked with Marino as an assistant director on some of his films such as ''[[Il Mio amico Jekyll]]'' and later directed under the name [[Romolo  Guerrieri]].{{sfn|Curti|2015|p=56}} Marino Girolami is also the father of actor [[Ennio Girolami]] and director [[Enzo G. Castellari]].{{sfn|Curti|2015|p=56}}

